contract:
Issue #36 (P3) Done when:
- A missing file under /assets/ (or any path with a file extension) gets a 404, not the HTML page; hashed build files are cached long-term; index.html is not. Dotfiles in the build folder are not served (NFR-13).
- On the real Render instance, the bot's reply time is measured against NFR-2/NFR-3; if it misses, the engine thread count can be set for the deploy (for example an env override) and is set to fit the instance. (The measurement and setting the value on Render are the coordinator's, after deploy. Your part is the override.)
Facts at base 0215881:
- apps/server/src/app.ts:145-159:
  const webDist = deps.webDist;
  if (webDist !== undefined) { checkWebDist(webDist); void app.register(fastifyStatic, { root: webDist }); }
  app.setNotFoundHandler((request, reply) => {
    const method = request.method;
    if (webDist !== undefined && (method === "GET" || method === "HEAD") && !isApiPath(request.url)) {
      return reply.status(200).sendFile("index.html");
    }
    return reply.status(404).send(apiError(`no route ${method} ${request.url}`));
  });
- apps/server/test/deploy.test.ts: "SPA fallback: an unknown non-/api GET returns index.html" currently asserts 200 index.html for ["/games/abc", "/games/abc?x=1", "/assets/missing.js", "/apifoo"]; /assets/missing.js must move to the 404 expectation. The fixture serves /assets/app.js (currently cache-control "public, max-age=0").
- @fastify/static has options such as dotfiles, setHeaders(res, path), cacheControl/maxAge/immutable. Check the installed version's options in node_modules before relying on them.
- apps/server/src/config.ts:27: export function loadEngineThreads(path = TUTOR_CONFIG_PATH): number | undefined { return readConfig(path).engine?.threads; }  Called from apps/server/src/main.ts:93 as loadEngineThreads() with no argument. main.ts is touched by open PR #79, so DO NOT edit main.ts: add an optional second parameter env: Record<string, string | undefined> = process.env to loadEngineThreads so the call site stays unchanged.
- config/tutor.json: "engine": { "flavor": "full", "threads": 4, "depth": 18, "movetimeCapMs": 1000, "multiPv": 3 }. render.yaml (plan: starter) and config/ are coordinator-owned.
- Not in scope (noted in the issue, not filed): HEAD fallback tests, SSE with WEB_DIST, /API/x case.
